---
<p class="lead">Published in 1995 to mark twenty-five years of Just Jeans, commissioned by founder Craig Kimberley and researched and written by Keith Dunstan.</p>
<hr>
<div class="row">
  <div class="col-12 col-md-3">
    <img src="{{ '/img/justjeansthestory.jpg' | url }}" class="img-fluid" alt="Cover of the book">
  </div>
  <div class="col-12 col-md-9">
    <h3 class="h5">From the back cover</h3>
    <p>This is the story of denim, the story of jeans, a fabric that first caught the imagination of Californian miners, cowboys and, in the 1960s, the rebellious young. Boosted by Hollywood, the craze spread until, finally, jeans became the uniform everywhere. They were the most loved garment the world had ever seen.</p>
    <p>But this is also a success story, a tale of two brothers who married two sisters. The Kimberleys began without even a motor car. They had a working capital of only $4,800 and a hand-decorated, leased shop in Melbourne's Chapel Street, Prahran. They sold just jeans. It was precisely the right time to do it. They caught a mood and a feeling. In 25 years the first Just Jeans store grew to nigh on 400 across Australia and New Zealand. Everybody now has at least two, if not three, pairs of jeans.</p>
  </div>
</div>
